# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the project tarball reached 149 MB and an upload died
# mid-transfer with ECONNRESET, after 44 s of compressing, on every attempt.
# Only ~39 MB of this repo is app source; the rest is screenshots, .docx manuals,
# the Odoo server addon and a git worktree — none of it referenced by app.json,
# the config plugins or the bundle. Excluding it takes the archive to single-digit
# MB, which compresses in seconds and survives a flaky connection.
#
# THE TRAP: once this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in
# addition to it. Everything that must stay out has to be named here — above all
# node_modules/, which is 521 MB. Forget that one line and the upload gets
# thirteen times worse, not better. Same for the secrets at the bottom: they are
# covered by .gitignore today and would otherwise start being uploaded.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's, which means a `#` only starts a comment at the START of
# a line. A trailing comment becomes part of the pattern and the rule silently
# matches nothing — so every note here is on its own line.

# ---- Dependencies and generated native projects: EAS makes these itself ----
node_modules/
# 186 MB, and the build has no use for history. EAS is understood to skip it
# anyway; named explicitly because it is the single largest thing here and
# "understood to" is not worth 186 MB.
.git/
/android
/ios
.expo/
dist/
web-build/

# ---- Not part of building the Android app ----
# 51 MB of device captures from test sessions
screenshots/
# 15 MB of .docx manuals and their screenshots
documents/
# the Odoo server addon — backend, not the app
odoo_modules/
# agent state, and worktrees: a second full copy of the app
.claude/
ui-artifacts/
coverage/
.maestro/
SESSION_*.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.zip

# ---- Secrets. Restated because .gitignore no longer applies. ----
credentials.json
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
.env*.local

# ---- Deliberately NOT excluded, each for a reason ----
# google-services.json  ships inside the APK; excluding it breaks the build
#                       (see the note in .gitignore)
# assets/               icons, splash and fonts referenced from app.json
# modules/              the local expo-task-widget-bridge module, autolinked
# plugins/              the four config plugins app.json names — withNotifeeRepo
#                       among them, without which app.notifee:core will not resolve
